  "verdict": "POSITIVE (diversification), in-sample structural: the min-variance blend cuts query-risk to 0.067, below the least-risky single architecture (0.076), with diversification ratio 1.29>1; it Pareto-dominates 8/11 single architectures and 10/11 single architectures are Pareto-inefficient (some blend matches their mean at lower risk). The tangency blend lifts in-sample Sharpe +13.2% over the best single arch (base_p4). Top-tier arms are only 0.46 mean-correlated, so the diversification headroom is genuine. OUT-OF-SAMPLE (leave-one-source-out): the min-variance blend's diversification ratio stays >1 in every fold (mean 1.494, min 1.2291) and its risk is below the least-risky single arch in 3/5 folds; the max-Sharpe tangency blend OVERFITS (median OOS Sharpe improvement 0.0846>0, but mean -4.2479 is dragged negative by the two smallest folds). Robust claim: blending lowers query-risk without sacrificing mean; chasing the max-Sharpe frontier point does not transfer."
 },
