  "threshold_sensitivity_note": "PRIMARY uses a prevalence-matched vote rule (top-k flagged correct, k from the gold base rate) - it does NOT peek at which reports are gold-correct, so it is the apples-to-apples analogue of E3's raw-verdict phi and gives two-Claude error-corr 0.52 (vs E3 phi_opus|sonnet 0.512) and N_eff 1.57 (vs E3 1.65). The Youden robustness fits each judge's threshold SEPARATELY to gold, which mechanically decorrelates their errors (two-Claude corr drops to 0.03) and inflates N_eff to 1.80; N_eff stays well below 3 either way, but the correlated structure that corroborates n_eff is the non-gold-peeking (primary) rule.",
  "verdict": "CORROBORATES n_eff: the two Claude judges are the most error-correlated pair (rho=0.52, vs the cross-family pairs), and the correlated-CJT effective independent-judge count is 1.57 (CI [1.4293, 1.7744]) - far below 3 and consistent with the independent E3 estimate n_eff=1.65. The beta-binomial correlated model predicts the observed 3-judge-majority-vs-gold accuracy (|err|=0.004) far better than the naive-independent CJT (|err|=0.055), confirming the votes are positively correlated, not independent."
 },
